PATH RECONCILIATION (binding, honest)
  The generated prompt's templated Output/Allowed path
  `apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Settings/**` does NOT exist in the project and
  is NOT compiled by project.yml. Every shipped P7 page lives under
  `apps/apple/Sources/Features/<Category>/` (ApiPlayground, AuditLog, DevTools…),
  and project.yml compiles `Sources/`. The page is therefore implemented at the
  REAL, compiled convention: apps/apple/Sources/Features/Settings/**. Navigation
  registration (AppRoute/AppRouteParser/TeslaSyncApp) and the string catalog are
  the prompt's other allowed surfaces.

SCOPE (honesty covenant: no scope-narrowing, no stubs as final, ADR-011)
  The web source ActiveSessionsPage.tsx wraps <ActiveSessionsSection/>. The thin
  page manifest record lists only the 2 page strings, but a title-only screen
  would be a stub. The FULL functional surface is reproduced natively: loading
  branch, AUTH_MODE_OPEN advisory, forward-auth session list (device + IP +
  signed-in + last-seen + "this device" badge), per-row "Sign out" and bulk
  "Sign out all other devices", each behind a destructive confirmation
  (web ConfirmDialog, no silence key), plus empty + error(retry) states.
  (The web ActiveSessionsSection *component* is separately ported in the
  experimental tree apps/apple/TeslaSync/feature-views/ActiveSessionsSection.*
  using distinct types — no collision; this P7 PAGE is self-contained per the
  canonical page pattern.)

